1
00:00:00,777 --> 00:00:09,157
I found myself lost and alone on this journey

2
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:17,497
Though my heart wandered far and wide, I could move not an inch

3
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:22,587
But now I can depart for any distant land

4
00:00:22,587 --> 00:00:25,717
But now I can depart for any distant land

5
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:28,757
Now that we've met on this road

6
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:34,557
Now that we've met on this road

7
00:00:35,057 --> 00:00:42,397
Even the unfamiliar songs of travelers

8
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:53,157
Can spark nostalgia in me when I'm with you

9
00:00:53,157 --> 00:00:57,037
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

10
00:00:57,037 --> 00:01:01,417
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

11
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:09,847
Then let's go search for it beyond the wind

12
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:13,807
Through chilling dawns,

13
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:18,227
Through arid noons,

14
00:01:18,227 --> 00:01:22,187
Through shivering nights,

15
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:28,197
Let's go see what lies at the end

16
00:01:41,707 --> 00:01:46,707
Wolf and a New Journey

17
00:02:02,527 --> 00:02:06,817
I thought our next meeting would be a tearful reunion. What a miserable sight.

18
00:02:08,067 --> 00:02:09,907
They set us up.

19
00:02:09,907 --> 00:02:11,487
This was the only thing I could protect.

20
00:02:12,197 --> 00:02:14,737
God, you're a fine fool.

21
00:02:15,327 --> 00:02:17,197
Face swollen from being beaten,

22
00:02:17,827 --> 00:02:20,617
covered in dirt, wrists burned by rope...

23
00:02:21,377 --> 00:02:24,327
And as you endure such humiliation,

24
00:02:24,667 --> 00:02:28,797
the whole time you're protecting my neatly folded cloak from the rain like your life depends on it?

25
00:02:29,627 --> 00:02:31,337
You're softhearted beyond belief!

26
00:02:33,547 --> 00:02:34,297
You know...

27
00:02:35,507 --> 00:02:38,097
I might be about to kill someone.

28
00:02:38,517 --> 00:02:39,727
Holo...

29
00:02:39,727 --> 00:02:46,607
I thought it was best to follow the plan and resume our journey as soon as possible,

30
00:02:46,607 --> 00:02:52,117
so I opted not to fight those pups and took a more civilized approach.

31
00:02:52,117 --> 00:02:55,357
Don't tell me that they made you...

32
00:02:55,357 --> 00:02:56,067
Don't say it!

33
00:02:58,287 --> 00:02:59,957
Forget about it.

34
00:02:59,957 --> 00:03:01,787
It was my own decision.

35
00:03:03,207 --> 00:03:05,657
But this is what I get in return?

36
00:03:06,167 --> 00:03:10,757
To accept what's happened to you is entirely beyond me!

37
00:03:12,757 --> 00:03:17,387
I'm going to find Lemerio and give him what he deserves.

38
00:03:18,137 --> 00:03:19,347
W-Wait a second.

39
00:03:19,347 --> 00:03:22,847
We have to take care of Liebert as soon as possible.

40
00:03:25,397 --> 00:03:27,857
I hope you have a good reason for this.

41
00:03:27,857 --> 00:03:30,817
They're going to kill Norah.

42
00:03:31,237 --> 00:03:33,317
That girl is with her partner.

43
00:03:33,317 --> 00:03:35,777
She'll probably be all right in any case.

44
00:03:35,777 --> 00:03:39,157
Partner? Sheep dogs can only do so much!

45
00:03:39,157 --> 00:03:40,247
You could...

46
00:03:40,247 --> 00:03:41,787
I could what?

47
00:03:41,787 --> 00:03:45,117
You could fight a hundred armed men without breaking a sweat.

48
00:03:45,127 --> 00:03:47,707
I'll be in my wolf form, you know!

49
00:03:48,707 --> 00:03:50,417
And that little girl is a shepherd!

50
00:03:58,967 --> 00:04:00,387
Even so... could you do it?

51
00:04:00,707 --> 00:04:05,687
An innocent person is about to die, and I can't just look the other way.

52
00:04:07,067 --> 00:04:08,607
I'll reward you handsomely.

53
00:04:09,537 --> 00:04:10,607
How?

54
00:04:10,607 --> 00:04:15,357
I'll do my best to grant any wish as long as you don't ask for Norah's life.

55
00:04:18,117 --> 00:04:18,867
Please.

56
00:04:20,657 --> 00:04:22,397
No one can stop this but you!

57
00:04:25,037 --> 00:04:26,247
Holo!

58
00:04:28,497 --> 00:04:31,167
I should take my clothes off, right?

59
00:04:31,167 --> 00:04:33,627
It'd be a shame to waste the time someone put into them.

60
00:04:33,627 --> 00:04:35,087
Are you going to do it?

61
00:04:35,087 --> 00:04:36,717
There's one condition.

62
00:04:37,137 --> 00:04:42,967
I can't guarantee the life of anyone who annoys me.

63
00:04:43,657 --> 00:04:45,637
Is that a deal?

64
00:04:45,637 --> 00:04:46,807
Do as you will if that happens.

65
00:04:47,857 --> 00:04:50,357
But I have faith in you.

66
00:04:54,647 --> 00:04:56,817
You certainly have found yourself a way with words.

67
00:04:57,867 --> 00:05:02,697
What a troublesome companion I've acquired.

68
00:05:04,577 --> 00:05:07,247
Now, isn't there something you want to say?

69
00:05:09,667 --> 00:05:11,087
Yes, it's a magnificent tail.

70
00:05:11,997 --> 00:05:14,997
It was a little forced, but it'll do for now.

71
00:05:15,007 --> 00:05:18,087
Now close your eyes for a moment.

72
00:05:23,597 --> 00:05:25,677
Here, hop on.

73
00:05:25,677 --> 00:05:27,177
You can hold on to my fur.

74
00:05:31,017 --> 00:05:33,647
I'm going to carry you in my mouth if you fall off.

75
00:05:33,647 --> 00:05:35,307
I'll hold on for dear life—

76
00:05:43,987 --> 00:05:44,997
Hey.

77
00:05:44,997 --> 00:05:45,867
What?

78
00:05:46,537 --> 00:05:51,337
I really detest shepherds, you know.

79
00:05:51,957 --> 00:05:53,837
I'm relieved to hear that.

80
00:05:53,837 --> 00:05:58,827
Norah's going to quit working as a shepherd regardless of whether this plan succeeds.

81
00:06:01,717 --> 00:06:03,717
I've decided on what I want.

82
00:06:03,717 --> 00:06:04,217
What is it?

83
00:06:04,657 --> 00:06:07,427
The finest peach preserves that money can buy!

84
00:06:07,427 --> 00:06:09,057
Well, just don't bankru—

85
00:06:10,227 --> 00:06:12,227
Lawrence-san and Holo-san?

86
00:06:12,227 --> 00:06:15,527
When we found them, it was already too late.

87
00:06:15,857 --> 00:06:18,357
We found them lying on top of each other.

88
00:06:19,987 --> 00:06:21,157
Norah-san!

89
00:06:22,197 --> 00:06:25,197
Sorry. I'm all right.

90
00:06:25,197 --> 00:06:27,707
No, I understand how terrible this must be for you.

91
00:06:28,327 --> 00:06:32,957
We have to pull ourselves together and fight to the end as those who survived.

92
00:06:32,957 --> 00:06:35,917
Are you ready for this?

93
00:06:35,917 --> 00:06:37,087
What?

94
00:06:37,087 --> 00:06:38,537
They're right over there.

95
00:06:38,547 --> 00:06:40,257
We've caught up to them already?

96
00:06:40,257 --> 00:06:41,127
Indeed.

97
00:06:41,797 --> 00:06:42,967
I can't see a thing.

98
00:06:43,757 --> 00:06:46,847
Those bastards are well-armed.

99
00:06:47,347 --> 00:06:48,887
There are around twenty of them.

100
00:06:48,887 --> 00:06:50,437
That many?

101
00:06:50,437 --> 00:06:52,477
It doesn't matter. Leave it all to me.

102
00:06:58,987 --> 00:07:01,487
I'm going to lay low after I leap over them.

103
00:07:01,487 --> 00:07:03,107
Jump off when I do.

104
00:07:16,497 --> 00:07:18,047
You mustn't get close.

105
00:07:20,337 --> 00:07:21,957
Protect the shepherd and the sheep!

106
00:07:25,217 --> 00:07:26,137
Norah!

107
00:07:26,757 --> 00:07:27,717
She was safe after all.

108
00:07:40,857 --> 00:07:42,267
Take the shepherd and run!

109
00:07:42,697 --> 00:07:43,967
Now!

110
00:07:46,927 --> 00:07:48,157
Shepherd!

111
00:07:48,827 --> 00:07:50,247
Protect me!

112
00:07:57,097 --> 00:07:58,127
Enek...

113
00:08:01,717 --> 00:08:02,537
This isn't good.

114
00:08:03,257 --> 00:08:04,797
Holo's serious.

115
00:08:04,797 --> 00:08:09,097
I'll give you three hundred Lumione if you protect me.

116
00:08:19,317 --> 00:08:20,607
No...

117
00:08:22,817 --> 00:08:24,067
Enek!

118
00:08:55,767 --> 00:08:57,057
Enek!

119
00:08:57,057 --> 00:08:58,107
Wait!

120
00:09:10,697 --> 00:09:11,947
Norah-san!

121
00:09:15,997 --> 00:09:16,947
Um...

122
00:09:16,947 --> 00:09:17,957
Yes?

123
00:09:17,957 --> 00:09:21,077
You're not a ghost, are you?

124
00:09:33,627 --> 00:09:35,217
Let me reveal the trick.

125
00:09:37,087 --> 00:09:39,097
That wolf is Holo.

126
00:09:41,977 --> 00:09:43,727
Holo... san?

127
00:09:44,277 --> 00:09:45,687
You didn't kill him?

128
00:09:46,857 --> 00:09:52,357
I was going to swallow him whole, but the gold he was carrying would have upset my stomach.

129
00:09:52,357 --> 00:09:53,857
I see.

130
00:09:55,617 --> 00:09:56,577
This is it.

131
00:10:04,947 --> 00:10:08,297
Fiends! Do you think you're going to get away with this?

132
00:10:09,507 --> 00:10:11,967
Good day, Liebert-san.

133
00:10:13,747 --> 00:10:15,547
I wasn't the one who betrayed you.

134
00:10:15,547 --> 00:10:18,557
Believe me... I didn't... I didn't...

135
00:10:18,557 --> 00:10:21,767
This wolf has been summoned as a messenger of the one and only God.

136
00:10:22,307 --> 00:10:24,017
Lies will do you no good here.

137
00:10:27,377 --> 00:10:30,817
The cut you asked for was too much!

138
00:10:30,817 --> 00:10:34,287
If we went along, we'd only be able to pay off our debts without making a profit.

139
00:10:34,287 --> 00:10:37,657
That's why Lemerio asked me to do something about it.

140
00:10:37,657 --> 00:10:39,117
You understand, don't you?

141
00:10:39,117 --> 00:10:41,447
We're both merchants, after all...

142
00:10:42,347 --> 00:10:43,767
Don't bring me down to your level!

143
00:10:44,877 --> 00:10:47,007
Sorry about the trouble.

144
00:10:47,007 --> 00:10:49,337
Oh, that's... okay...

145
00:10:49,337 --> 00:10:52,757
Long story short, Lemerio Trading betrayed us.

146
00:10:53,597 --> 00:10:56,297
They were planning to kill you, too.

147
00:10:59,157 --> 00:11:02,217
I had a feeling something wasn't right, but...

148
00:11:03,267 --> 00:11:06,187
Let's run away with the gold.

149
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:09,027
Let's see.

150
00:11:09,857 --> 00:11:15,397
We have six hundred Lumione worth of gold even without having to resort to smuggling.

151
00:11:15,947 --> 00:11:19,907
If we ignore those traitors at Lemerio Trading and split the gold amongst ourselves,

152
00:11:19,907 --> 00:11:21,367
we'll have enough to live in luxury.

153
00:11:21,757 --> 00:11:26,977
On the other hand, we wouldn't have been able to buy the gold without their contribution.

154
00:11:27,537 --> 00:11:33,277
If we run away with the gold, they'll go bankrupt and end up on the streets with certainty.

155
00:11:33,277 --> 00:11:34,257
That's why...

156
00:11:35,217 --> 00:11:36,377
That's why...

157
00:11:39,847 --> 00:11:40,387
Holo!

158
00:11:42,387 --> 00:11:45,977
We still have to live our lives after this.

159
00:11:46,357 --> 00:11:50,647
There won't be an end to this grudge if we take revenge for their betrayal.

160
00:11:50,647 --> 00:11:51,857
In that case...

161
00:11:51,857 --> 00:11:55,407
And don't say you'll kill every last one of them!

162
00:11:55,397 --> 00:12:00,317
I don't want the bread I buy tomorrow to have been paid for in blood.

163
00:12:00,317 --> 00:12:03,537
There are many ways to end this.

164
00:12:04,037 --> 00:12:07,157
Don't you want to make a decision that'll lead to a brighter future?

165
00:12:09,127 --> 00:12:13,587
Holo, if it weren't for you, I'd be freezing to death by the forest right now.

166
00:12:13,967 --> 00:12:17,047
I owe you my gratitude for listening to my selfish request.

167
00:12:17,047 --> 00:12:17,807
But...

168
00:12:17,807 --> 00:12:20,757
Enough. Do whatever you want.

169
00:12:20,757 --> 00:12:24,597
Ah, my travel companion is tiresome beyond words!

170
00:12:26,937 --> 00:12:28,397
Sorry to keep you waiting.

171
00:12:28,397 --> 00:12:29,847
Not at all.

172
00:12:30,277 --> 00:12:32,517
I suggest we do the following.

173
00:12:36,477 --> 00:12:38,237
So...

174
00:12:38,237 --> 00:12:39,177
What?

175
00:12:39,627 --> 00:12:42,407
Might I hear the truth now?

176
00:12:42,407 --> 00:12:43,837
What are you talking about?

177
00:12:43,837 --> 00:12:45,327
Don't play dumb with me.

178
00:12:45,327 --> 00:12:48,197
There's a limit to how generous a person can be.

179
00:12:48,997 --> 00:12:53,377
You can decide whether you want to carry this gold into Lubinheigen.

180
00:12:54,577 --> 00:12:57,827
You could also settle for your fair share of this gold right here.

181
00:12:58,427 --> 00:12:59,217
I see.

182
00:12:59,217 --> 00:13:04,137
But if we can manage to smuggle it safely, its value will
increase to six thousand Lumione through my connections.

183
00:13:04,137 --> 00:13:05,847
S-Six thousand?

184
00:13:05,847 --> 00:13:10,147
We could save Lemerio Trading with that kind of money.

185
00:13:11,977 --> 00:13:13,897
I guess I can't hide anything from you.

186
00:13:13,897 --> 00:13:16,087
There wasn't enough gold.

187
00:13:17,357 --> 00:13:20,617
Six hundred Lumione was more than an exaggeration.

188
00:13:20,617 --> 00:13:21,647
It's a hundred at best.

189
00:13:22,197 --> 00:13:26,867
If you split the gold up, there wouldn't have been anything left after you paid your debt back.

190
00:13:26,867 --> 00:13:29,497
You would have had to carry out the smuggling to make a profit.

191
00:13:29,877 --> 00:13:32,577
Lemerio was in a desperate situation.

192
00:13:33,007 --> 00:13:37,957
They only managed to get one-sixth of the amount we had agreed upon.

193
00:13:38,297 --> 00:13:43,797
Once they got it inside, they probably could have gotten a thousand Lumione at most...

194
00:13:43,797 --> 00:13:49,437
...so they knew they wouldn't have enough to pay for our silence from the very beginning.

195
00:13:50,017 --> 00:13:54,687
It's probably why they agreed to our offer in the first place.

196
00:13:56,237 --> 00:13:58,737
All right. I understand the circumstances, but...

197
00:13:58,737 --> 00:14:00,567
Is anything else bothering you?

198
00:14:00,947 --> 00:14:05,127
You didn't have to lie like that for her sake.

199
00:14:05,907 --> 00:14:07,197
Was I being a showoff?

200
00:14:10,327 --> 00:14:12,867
You don't have to shoulder the burden by yourself.

201
00:14:17,587 --> 00:14:20,207
I still have other things on my mind, but...

202
00:14:21,347 --> 00:14:22,427
Get on.

203
00:14:23,177 --> 00:14:26,217
You have to find Lemerio, don't you?

204
00:14:26,977 --> 00:14:29,307
Aren't you coming with me?

205
00:14:29,647 --> 00:14:31,897
Matters of business don't concern me.

206
00:14:31,897 --> 00:14:33,317
Are you still upset?

207
00:14:34,527 --> 00:14:36,847
You're going to fall off if you don't hush.

208
00:14:49,157 --> 00:14:50,787
F-Five hundred?

209
00:14:51,167 --> 00:14:52,247
Yes.

210
00:14:52,877 --> 00:14:59,457
Should we succeed in smuggling the gold in,
we'd like you to buy it for five hundred Lumione.

211
00:14:59,457 --> 00:15:03,427
A-Absolutely not. Do you really think we have the funds to do that?

212
00:15:03,427 --> 00:15:06,057
I'm not asking you to pay in full right now.

213
00:15:06,377 --> 00:15:12,287
Sign a contract that will accommodate a gradual repayment of your debt within a period of ten years.

214
00:15:12,287 --> 00:15:14,687
Five hundred is still out of the question.

215
00:15:14,687 --> 00:15:20,147
You're the one who created a trading company that had the most impressive dock in town.

216
00:15:20,147 --> 00:15:23,197
Five hundred Lumione in ten years must be child's play to you.

217
00:15:23,197 --> 00:15:24,447
W-What are you doing?

218
00:15:24,777 --> 00:15:26,937
I heard everything from Liebert-san.

219
00:15:32,417 --> 00:15:35,497
Instead of running away with a paltry amount of money,

220
00:15:35,917 --> 00:15:40,457
I'm sure it's in your best interests to concede to our demands and attempt to revive your company.

221
00:15:41,007 --> 00:15:44,467
The bearer of the deed will be the Lohen Trading Union.

222
00:15:44,467 --> 00:15:45,627
The union?

223
00:15:46,007 --> 00:15:48,297
You might be able to betray a private trader like myself,

224
00:15:48,297 --> 00:15:52,597
but you won't be able to get away with doing the same thing to a trading union.

225
00:15:52,597 --> 00:15:55,557
I thought I'd never see you again!

226
00:15:55,557 --> 00:15:58,317
This is for making me worry!

227
00:15:58,317 --> 00:15:59,437
O-Ouch.

228
00:15:59,437 --> 00:16:02,447
You son of a gun!

229
00:16:02,447 --> 00:16:05,147
That's what you call filial devotion.

230
00:16:11,407 --> 00:16:17,087
So now you just sell this ten year contract to me and never have to deal with Lemerio again.

231
00:16:17,087 --> 00:16:18,787
How'd you do it?

232
00:16:19,267 --> 00:16:21,577
It was a simple gold transaction,

233
00:16:22,007 --> 00:16:23,877
but I can't tell you about the details.

234
00:16:25,007 --> 00:16:27,507
Well, I'll buy it for thirty.

235
00:16:27,507 --> 00:16:30,677
I'll pay an extra hundred if your deal goes through.

236
00:16:30,677 --> 00:16:31,767
A hundred?

237
00:16:31,767 --> 00:16:34,007
I'm in a cheerful mood. Think of it as a present.

238
00:16:35,267 --> 00:16:37,097
Thank you very much.

239
00:16:37,097 --> 00:16:41,687
That should be enough for me to cover all the apologies
and such I'll need to be making as well as my debt.

240
00:16:43,067 --> 00:16:47,197
You really have become a full-fledged merchant.

241
00:16:47,197 --> 00:16:50,607
Let's drink until we pass out as soon as I'm finished with work.

242
00:16:50,607 --> 00:16:53,037
Well, I'm not sure I...

243
00:16:53,867 --> 00:16:54,867
My companion...

244
00:16:55,867 --> 00:16:56,987
You're late.

245
00:16:56,987 --> 00:17:00,967
Sorry. What is it that you wanted to ask?

246
00:17:00,967 --> 00:17:02,397
I have two questions.

247
00:17:02,397 --> 00:17:03,547
Two?

248
00:17:03,547 --> 00:17:07,967
First, how much trust do you have in that girl?

249
00:17:08,847 --> 00:17:12,637
We can catch up to Norah if she tries to run away with the gold.

250
00:17:13,337 --> 00:17:17,517
I didn't hand her the gold out of blind faith.

251
00:17:17,517 --> 00:17:19,937
Well, I suppose that's that.

252
00:17:19,937 --> 00:17:21,437
Your next question?

253
00:17:21,977 --> 00:17:23,937
I'll answer anything you ask.

254
00:17:24,357 --> 00:17:27,527
I owe you at least that much.

255
00:17:27,527 --> 00:17:28,907
I...

256
00:17:30,297 --> 00:17:31,737
want to get some fresh air.

257
00:17:47,497 --> 00:17:51,127
Do you remember?

258
00:17:52,137 --> 00:17:57,137
Whose name did you call when I confronted the girl and the dog?

259
00:17:58,387 --> 00:18:01,387
I couldn't hear anything because I was caught up in the moment,

260
00:18:02,637 --> 00:18:06,947
but I'm sure you called out someone's name.

261
00:18:08,277 --> 00:18:09,487
Has it been eating at you?

262
00:18:09,487 --> 00:18:10,487
No...

263
00:18:11,407 --> 00:18:13,317
It's not that important.

264
00:18:42,897 --> 00:18:44,227
I called out to you.

265
00:18:52,827 --> 00:18:54,447
You just lied, didn't you?

266
00:18:54,827 --> 00:18:56,277
Yes I did.

267
00:18:56,697 --> 00:18:58,817
The truth is that I don't remember.

268
00:18:59,327 --> 00:19:00,367
But...

269
00:19:00,697 --> 00:19:02,287
But?

270
00:19:02,287 --> 00:19:06,627
I must have called out to you if I take the circumstances into consideration.

271
00:19:06,627 --> 00:19:09,007
It was a critical situation.

272
00:19:09,007 --> 00:19:12,707
There's no doubt I would have instinctively chosen to call your name.

273
00:19:13,217 --> 00:19:14,127
After all...

274
00:19:14,137 --> 00:19:15,547
W-Wait!

275
00:19:21,267 --> 00:19:23,137
All right. Go ahead.

276
00:19:25,847 --> 00:19:26,937
After all...

277
00:19:28,857 --> 00:19:32,187
Your name isn't as long as hers.

278
00:19:42,417 --> 00:19:45,927
And if I'd said "Norah," it still would have been distinct even if I said it quickly.

279
00:19:46,587 --> 00:19:49,417
On the other hand, I could have said Holo in less than a second.

280
00:19:49,417 --> 00:19:52,207
It's entirely plausible that you could miss it if you were distracted.

281
00:19:52,837 --> 00:19:55,257
What do you think? Pretty convincing, isn't it?

282
00:19:55,257 --> 00:19:56,307
Shut up!

283
00:19:56,307 --> 00:19:59,137
You called out my name because it isn't as long?

284
00:19:59,137 --> 00:20:00,177
You fool!

285
00:20:00,597 --> 00:20:04,787
What upsets me even more is the fact that you sincerely believe that!

286
00:20:05,377 --> 00:20:11,317
I could have scratched you up to my heart's content if you had said you called out to that girl!

287
00:20:20,187 --> 00:20:20,947
Fine.

288
00:20:21,497 --> 00:20:23,327
I'll give you another chance.

289
00:20:24,827 --> 00:20:26,907
Call out my name.

290
00:21:27,057 --> 00:21:27,977
Holo.

291
00:21:29,397 --> 00:21:31,307
It really is easy to say.

292
00:21:33,527 --> 00:21:34,267
You fool!

293
00:21:41,397 --> 00:21:43,197
Oh, that's right.

294
00:21:43,197 --> 00:21:45,367
I owe you an explanation.

295
00:21:46,667 --> 00:21:49,037
He was never in love with me.

296
00:21:49,587 --> 00:21:52,117
He had just realized what I was.

297
00:21:52,457 --> 00:21:54,337
I see.

298
00:21:55,377 --> 00:21:57,377
He's a wonderful partner.

299
00:21:57,757 --> 00:22:00,427
Much more useful than this man over here.

300
00:22:00,427 --> 00:22:01,877
Don't get carried away.

301
00:22:03,807 --> 00:22:06,347
I hope you two find happiness.

302
00:22:11,727 --> 00:22:20,107
I found myself lost and alone on this journey

303
00:22:20,107 --> 00:22:28,447
Though my heart wandered far and wide, I could move not an inch

304
00:22:28,447 --> 00:22:36,667
But now I can depart for any distant land

305
00:22:36,667 --> 00:22:45,387
Now that we've met on this road

306
00:22:45,927 --> 00:22:53,577
Even the unfamiliar songs of travelers

307
00:22:53,577 --> 00:23:03,887
Can spark nostalgia in me when I'm with you

308
00:23:03,887 --> 00:23:12,427
If I could take your outstretched hand

309
00:23:12,427 --> 00:23:20,807
Then how far could we go?

310
00:23:20,807 --> 00:23:29,017
Let's set off to wherever we please

311
00:23:29,017 --> 00:23:38,647
And bask in the sounds and smells of unfamiliar lands

